Goal: Finalize and validate the existing uncommitted work in this repository: a fix for DOG-035 (see the DOG-035 entry in dogfood/findings/FINDINGS.md). `orchestrate --verify` used argparse nargs="+", so a verification command with its own flags (for example `--verify python3 -m unittest`) failed with "unrecognized arguments". The uncommitted change adds `verification_command()` in src/howlplane/control_plane/orchestration.py (shell-splits a single quoted command for new sessions, resume and Factory queue tasks), a quoting hint in src/howlplane/control_plane/cli.py main(), documentation in documentation/ORCHESTRATE.md and change_log.md, and tests in tests/test_orchestration_verification_rework.py.

If the existing change is correct and complete, report IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS: NO_CHANGE_REQUIRED with reasons; otherwise fix only what is wrong. Reviewers: try to falsify the fix. Check every path that consumes --verify (new session, resume, Factory queue tasks), whether shell-splitting a single token can mis-split a legitimate one-token command (for example a path containing spaces), whether switching cli.main from parse_args to parse_known_args changes behavior for any other subcommand, whether the documentation now makes a claim the code does not keep, and whether the tests would fail without the fix.
